export const title = "MQTT Publish";
export const html = "<h1>MQTT Publish</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>You can use the Publish feature of <a href=\"https://mqtt.org/\">MQTT</a> to link AI Bridge with a range of devices.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 460\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"200\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"95\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\" font-weight=\"700\">AI Bridge device</text>\n  <text x=\"95\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\">Publish AI Events via MQTT topic</text>\n\n  <circle cx=\"345\" cy=\"235\" r=\"55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"345\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"24\">&#9729;&#65039;</text>\n  <text x=\"345\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#5b6270\" font-weight=\"700\">MQTT Broker</text>\n  <line x1=\"170\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n\n  <rect x=\"500\" y=\"30\" width=\"270\" height=\"380\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"420\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Subscribe</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"26\">&#128241;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Mobile App notification</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"26\">&#128250;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">VMS</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"26\">&#9729;&#65039;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">IoT cloud Apps</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"26\">&#128190;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Record on Storage</text>\n  <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"290\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"235\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"360\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrM)\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrM\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The AI Bridge device publishes AI events via an MQTT topic; subscribers can act on them</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>1. What is MQTT?</h2>\n<p>MQTT (Message Queuing Telemetry Transport) is a lightweight messaging protocol that enables efficient communication over low-bandwidth or unstable networks, such as those used by IoT devices. MQTT is used especially for delivering messages between connected devices at remote locations.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Characteristics of MQTT</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Lightweight protocol</strong> &ndash; MQTT is effective in environments with limited network bandwidth and resources.</li>\n<li><strong>Asynchronous communication</strong> &ndash; clients can send a message and receive messages later.</li>\n<li><strong>Quality of Service (QoS) levels</strong> &ndash; MQTT provides several QoS levels to guarantee message delivery reliability.</li>\n<li><strong>Last Will and Testament (LWT) message</strong> &ndash; a message delivered when a client disconnects abnormally.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Key Components of MQTT</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Broker</strong> &ndash; the server that relays messages between clients. It receives messages from a client and delivers them to other clients subscribed to the relevant topic. The broker is usually a centralized server and acts as the hub for every message exchange.</li>\n<li><strong>Client</strong> &ndash; an endpoint that sends and receives messages. A client can publish messages to the broker or subscribe to a specific topic. Clients can take many forms &ndash; IoT devices, mobile apps, server applications, and more.</li>\n<li><strong>Topic</strong> &ndash; defines how messages are classified. Topics are strings and can have a hierarchical structure (e.g. \"home/livingroom/temperature\"). A client subscribes to the specific topics it's interested in, and only receives messages for those topics.</li>\n<li><strong>Message Payload</strong> &ndash; the actual data portion of an MQTT message. The payload can be text, binary data, or other formats, and its size depends on the broker's implementation. The message payload contains the data a client wants to deliver to other clients.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. Configuring an MQTT Publish Action</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>MQTT Publish</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Set the action type to <strong>MQTT Publish</strong>, then click the Add button to display the related settings.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Topic Settings</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"max-width:560px;\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr auto;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Topic</span><input value=\"{{DEVICE NAME}}-{{CH}}\" disabled><span class=\"btn small primary\">Add</span>\n    <span>Topic Example</span><span style=\"grid-column:span 2;font-family:monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Device-3</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Topic setting &ndash; a fixed phrase or predefined tokens can be used</figcaption>\n</div>\n<p>Configure the topic. You can enter a fixed phrase, or combine it with predefined tokens, such as <strong>DEVICE NAME</strong>, <strong>MAC</strong>, <strong>CH</strong>, <strong>CH NAME</strong>, <strong>EVENT TYPE</strong>, and <strong>EVENT NAME</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Message Payload Settings</h3>\n<p>You can configure the Message Payload and set the QoS level.</p>\n<p>For how to set up the message payload, see the <a href=\"/meta-token-guide\">Event Meta Token &amp; Action Message Guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">MQTT Broker Settings</h3>\n<p>You can add an MQTT Broker, or choose which broker to use from among the brokers you've already added.</p>\n<p>Clicking the <strong>Add</strong> button displays the menu for adding an MQTT Broker.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:420px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">MQTT Broker</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Name</span><input placeholder=\"My Broker\" disabled>\n      <span>Host</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Port</span><input value=\"1883\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Adding an MQTT Broker</figcaption>\n</div>\n<p>You can set the MQTT Broker's name, along with its connection information. Check with the party responsible for the MQTT Broker for the connection details you need to enter.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Testing an MQTT Publish Action</h2>\n<p>Here's how to test using a free MQTT Broker and MQTT Web Client provided by <a href=\"https://www.hivemq.com/mqtt/public-mqtt-broker/\">HiveMQ</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">MQTT Client: Subscribe Settings</h3>\n<p>Go to HiveMQ's <a href=\"https://www.hivemq.com/demos/websocket-client/\">MQTT Web Client</a>. The connection settings for HiveMQ's free broker are pre-filled by default, so just click the <strong>Connect</strong> button.</p>\n<p>Once connected, click <strong>Add New Topic Subscription</strong> and enter the topic name you'll configure in the MQTT Publish action (e.g. \"ACTION_TEST_MQTT_PUBLISH\").</p>\n<p>Once configured, you'll see a page like the one below. Test results appear in this page's Message field, so check it after configuring the MQTT Publish action.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">MQTT Publish Action Settings</h3>\n<p>Configure the MQTT Publish action as shown below, and configure the MQTT Broker to point at the HiveMQ broker.</p>\n<p>After configuring it, click the <strong>Test</strong> button to run the MQTT Publish test action. Checking the MQTT Web Client shows the test result being received.</p>";
